============================================================

### SocketItemOption::Options ###
	Index      0-49, fixed - matches eSocketItemOption in SocketItemOption.h.
	           Do not renumber.
	Type       1 Fire, 2 Water, 3 Ice, 4 Wind, 5 Lightning, 6 Earth.
	SubIndex   Position of this option within its Type (0-4).
	Name       Free-text label, for readability only.
	Rate       Roll weight/percent for this option.
	Value1-5   Bonus magnitude at socket levels 1 through 5.

### SocketItemOption::BonusOptions ###
	Index             0-49, fixed - matches eSocketItemBonusOption.
	MinItemSection/
	MaxItemSection    Item section range (0-15, see Item.xml) this bonus
	                  can apply to (e.g. 0-4 = all weapons, 6-12 = armor).
	Name              Free-text label, for readability only.
	Value             Bonus magnitude.
	ReqOptionType1-5  0 = unused slot. Otherwise, an elemental Type (see
	                  above) that must be present among the item's 5
	                  socket options for this bonus to activate.

### SocketItemOption::PackageOptions ###
	Index                    0-1, fixed - matches eSocketItemPackageOption.
	Name                     Free-text label, for readability only.
	Value                    Bonus magnitude.
	ReqOptionTypeCount1-6    Minimum number of BonusOptions of each of the
	                         6 elemental Types (Fire..Earth, in order) that
	                         must be simultaneously active across the
	                         player's equipment for this package to unlock.

STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

